{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And afterwards she shall be purified.</b> In the waters of a mikveh that contain forty [se'ah], and so our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: ״אך במי נדה יתחטא״ — waters in which the menstruant immerses; and it is written ״ורחץ את כל בשרו במים״, and our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: waters in which the entire body rises [i.e., fits] — and the Sages [decreed]: the waters of a mikveh, forty se'ah. And Scripture supports this from מי השלוח that flow slowly, which in gematria are forty."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:13.474751392Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}